# Per-MCP source clones — LOCAL WORKING COPIES ONLY, never tracked here.
#
# In the v1.1 per-repo model each MCP lives in its own public repo and
# `actions/checkout-mcp-source` clones it over pending-to-publish/<mcp>/ on every
# run, so nothing in CI depends on a copy committed here (every MCP in
# mcp-pipeline.yaml has a repo_url). Three of these directories used to be tracked
# as bare gitlinks (mode 160000) with no .gitmodules entry, which meant:
#   * `git status` was permanently dirty on a clean checkout,
#   * every actions/checkout step logged `fatal: No url found for submodule path
#     'pending-to-publish/<mcp>' in .gitmodules` and exited 128 (a warning),
#   * and a commit made from the pipeline repo captured a pointer instead of the
#     artifacts — the v1.0-model residue behind the /prep-mcp bug fixed in #241.
# Untracked in the same cleanup. tests/unit/ci/no-tracked-gitlinks.test.ts keeps it
# that way.
pending-to-publish/*/

# Local cache (e.g., pinned MCP schema fetched once and reused)
.cache/
